WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.321 --> 00:00:15.862
is everyone?"

2
00:00:16.502 --> 00:00:17.463
Jonathan Cho asked.

3
00:00:18.283 --> 00:00:21.025
He brushed his long black hair from his eyes so he could see better.

4
00:00:21.946 --> 00:00:24.688
He and his best friend, Carlos Ruiz, stood near the soccer field.

5
00:00:25.268 --> 00:00:26.970
They were looking for other thirteen-year-olds.

6
00:00:26.990 --> 00:00:30.172
"My mom told me our new soccer team was meeting here today."

7
00:00:31.112 --> 00:00:35.096
"My dad told me the same thing, but I don't see any other players," Carlos said.

8
00:00:35.116 --> 00:00:39.359
"Maybe we joined an invisible team by mistake," Jonathan joked.

9
00:00:39.379 --> 00:00:41.141
"Feel around for them."

10
00:00:42.082 --> 00:00:44.124
Carlos laughed and waved his hands through the air.

11
00:00:45.184 --> 00:00:47.246
Jonathan pretended to shake an invisible hand.

12
00:00:47.266 --> 00:00:49.248
"Hello, invisible teammate.

13
00:00:49.909 --> 00:00:50.609
Nice to see you.

14
00:00:51.430 --> 00:00:52.411
Or not see you."

15
00:00:54.212 --> 00:00:58.076
Carlos laughed again, which was one of the things that Jonathan liked best about his friend.

16
00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:01.141
Carlos understood Jonathan's strange sense of humor.

17
00:01:01.161 --> 00:01:04.563
"Hey, I think some people are at the other end of the park."

18
00:01:05.163 --> 00:01:05.883
Carlos pointed.

19
00:01:06.683 --> 00:01:08.464
Jonathan spotted a small group of guys.

20
00:01:08.484 --> 00:01:10.065
"That must be our team."

21
00:01:10.965 --> 00:01:12.686
Jonathan and Carlos hurried toward them.

22
00:01:15.808 --> 00:01:20.530
As they got closer, Jonathan recognized a few boys, including Aaron and Andrew Russell.

23
00:01:21.250 --> 00:01:23.091
They were twins who lived on Jonathan's street.

24
00:01:24.011 --> 00:01:25.572
Both of them were good soccer players.

25
00:01:26.620 --> 00:01:29.461
A tall, bald man stood with the group, frowning at a clipboard.

26
00:01:30.221 --> 00:01:31.822
Jonathan figured he was the coach.

27
00:01:31.842 --> 00:01:34.302
"See that guy on the left?"

28
00:01:34.822 --> 00:01:36.703
Carlos pointed to a lanky boy in the group.

29
00:01:36.723 --> 00:01:39.344
"Isn't that Max Wattenbarger?"

30
00:01:39.364 --> 00:01:40.664
"It is!

31
00:01:41.284 --> 00:01:42.765
Awesome!" Jonathan said.

32
00:01:43.745 --> 00:01:46.186
Max Wattenbarger was an excellent soccer player.

33
00:01:47.106 --> 00:01:49.306
He and Jonathan both played the position of forward.

34
00:01:49.987 --> 00:01:52.107
Working together, they could score a lot of goals.

35
00:01:53.047 --> 00:01:58.594
Jonathan played in the recreational league, which focused on having fun, improving skills, and letting everyone play.

36
00:01:59.454 --> 00:02:00.594
That was fine with Jonathan.

37
00:02:01.235 --> 00:02:05.056
He loved running outside on the grass, trying to become a better player, and being part of a

38
00:02:05.116 --> 00:02:08.558
team. Of course, Jonathan liked winning much more than losing.

39
00:02:09.338 --> 00:02:11.899
He'd bet he'd win a lot with Max Wattenbarger on his team.

40
00:02:13.260 --> 00:02:18.442
While Carlos talked to the twins, Jonathan went over to Max, who was expertly juggling a soccer ball

41
00:02:18.462 --> 00:02:18.962
with his feet.

42
00:02:18.982 --> 00:02:21.703
"Hey, Max.

43
00:02:21.943 --> 00:02:22.503
I'm Jonathan."

44
00:02:23.084 --> 00:02:23.504
He grinned.

45
00:02:24.204 --> 00:02:27.025
"This is the first time I'm actually happy to see you with a soccer ball!"

46
00:02:27.966 --> 00:02:29.526
"Huh?" Max frowned.

47
00:02:29.546 --> 00:02:32.207
"I was kidding," Jonathan said quickly.

48
00:02:32.227 --> 00:02:35.369
"I meant you're such a good player that it's tough to play against you.

49
00:02:35.909 --> 00:02:37.410
We've never been on the same team before."

50
00:02:38.350 --> 00:02:39.931
The coach stepped closer to Jonathan.

51
00:02:39.951 --> 00:02:43.652
"Max isn't just a good player.

52
00:02:44.372 --> 00:02:45.313
He's a great player.

53
00:02:45.953 --> 00:02:46.934
He learned from the best."

54
00:02:48.034 --> 00:02:49.114
"From Lionel Messi?"

55
00:02:49.595 --> 00:02:50.295
Jonathan joked.

56
00:02:50.935 --> 00:02:52.496
Neither Max nor the coach smiled.

57
00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:56.702
"I was joking again," Jonathan explained to them.

58
00:02:57.222 --> 00:02:59.323
But they didn't seem to get Jonathan's sense of humor.

59
00:03:00.444 --> 00:03:01.464
Now the coach was scowling.

60
00:03:01.484 --> 00:03:06.967
"If you spent more time practicing soccer skills and less time trying to be funny, maybe you'd be

61
00:03:06.987 --> 00:03:08.989
a great player like Max," he said.

62
00:03:09.009 --> 00:03:10.710
"I should know what it takes.

63
00:03:11.350 --> 00:03:14.112
I've been training Max for soccer stardom since he was three years old.

64
00:03:15.072 --> 00:03:17.213
I'm Max's father—and your new coach."

65
00:03:18.074 --> 00:03:18.874
Jonathan gulped.

66
00:03:20.015 --> 00:03:21.556
Coach Wattenbarger seemed stern.

67
00:03:22.176 --> 00:03:24.317
He obviously took soccer very seriously.

68
00:03:24.337 --> 00:03:26.338
"It's nice to meet you, Coach.

69
00:03:26.618 --> 00:03:30.499
I'm Jon—" "We're wasting time," the coach interrupted him.

70
00:03:31.200 --> 00:03:33.761
Then he said in a booming voice, "Listen up, everyone!

71
00:03:34.361 --> 00:03:35.461
I'm Coach Wattenbarger.

72
00:03:36.382 --> 00:03:39.483
I'll keep this meeting short so we can start practicing as soon as possible.

73
00:03:40.143 --> 00:03:41.464
You don't need to introduce yourselves.

74
00:03:42.384 --> 00:03:44.285
Just know who I am and who Max is."

75
00:03:45.165 --> 00:03:46.706
He clapped a hand on Max's shoulder.

76
00:03:46.726 --> 00:03:48.667
"He's my son.

77
00:03:49.327 --> 00:03:51.568
More importantly, he's the best player in the league.

78
00:03:52.236 --> 00:03:55.519
With Max on our team, I expect us to win every game!"

79
00:03:56.360 --> 00:03:57.200
The boys cheered.

80
00:03:59.462 --> 00:04:01.764
Coach Wattenbarger held up his hand to silence them.

81
00:04:01.784 --> 00:04:05.988
"We'll quickly vote on a team name, hold practice, and then hand out uniforms.

82
00:04:07.088 --> 00:04:08.470
Our uniforms are red, by the way.

83
00:04:09.030 --> 00:04:10.411
Let's pick our team's name fast."

84
00:04:11.852 --> 00:04:13.294
Jonathan liked choosing team names.

85
00:04:13.314 --> 00:04:15.355
"How about the Red Hot Suns?"

86
00:04:15.375 --> 00:04:18.498
"Or the Dragons," Carlos said.

87
00:04:18.518 --> 00:04:22.528
Aaron said, "How about—" "We're wasting time.

88
00:04:23.188 --> 00:04:25.049
Picking a team name won't help us win.

89
00:04:25.629 --> 00:04:28.370
Practice will help us win," Coach Wattenbarger said.

90
00:04:28.390 --> 00:04:29.990
"It's time to vote.

91
00:04:30.590 --> 00:04:32.631
Raise your hand if you like the name Max Attacks."

92
00:04:32.651 --> 00:04:38.112
"But What about—" A couple of kids tried to protest, but the coach cut them off.

93
00:04:38.132 --> 00:04:41.113
"Who votes for the name Team Mighty Max?"

94
00:04:41.733 --> 00:04:42.193
he asked.

95
00:04:42.894 --> 00:04:44.294
Again, no one raised his hand.

96
00:04:44.314 --> 00:04:48.575
"The final choice is Team Wattenbarger," the coach said.

97
00:04:49.575 --> 00:04:51.316
Only Max Wattenbarger raised his hand.

98
00:04:52.736 --> 00:04:56.599
"Team Wattenbarger got the most votes, so our name will be Team Wattenbarger!"

99
00:04:57.140 --> 00:04:57.841
the coach barked.

100
00:04:57.861 --> 00:05:01.904
"This is more like 'Team What a Bummer,'" Jonathan thought.

101
00:05:02.545 --> 00:05:04.726
He'd wanted a name to go with the team's red uniforms.

102
00:05:05.927 --> 00:05:07.949
Anything would be better than Team Wattenbarger.

103
00:05:08.510 --> 00:05:10.271
Well, not the Big Red Pimples.

104
00:05:10.491 --> 00:05:11.692
Or the Itchy Red Rashes.

105
00:05:12.653 --> 00:05:15.175
Still, Team Wattenbarger was an awful name.

106
00:05:16.216 --> 00:05:17.257
Jonathan raised his hand.

107
00:05:17.277 --> 00:05:20.300
"Coach, how about the Red Lightning Bolts?"

108
00:05:21.396 --> 00:05:22.836
The coach glanced up at the sky.

109
00:05:22.856 --> 00:05:24.637
"I don't see any lightning bolts.

110
00:05:25.497 --> 00:05:26.297
Time for practice!"

111
00:05:28.238 --> 00:05:29.598
The coach set up the first drill.

112
00:05:30.178 --> 00:05:32.459
Everyone had to take turns passing the ball to Max.

113
00:05:35.260 --> 00:05:38.241
Then Max got to dribble the ball down the field and shoot it into the goal.

114
00:05:42.942 --> 00:05:44.362
Max was an impressive player.

115
00:05:45.062 --> 00:05:47.563
He ran very fast and had excellent control of the ball.

116
00:05:48.423 --> 00:05:50.944
But Jonathan wished he and his teammates could practice shooting too.

117
00:05:52.196 --> 00:05:57.138
After an hour, which felt to Jonathan like ten hours, Coach Wattenbarger told everyone to drink some water

118
00:05:57.198 --> 00:05:58.179
and collect a uniform.

119
00:05:59.239 --> 00:06:01.760
Jonathan picked up his water bottle, but he wasn't thirsty.

120
00:06:02.460 --> 00:06:05.902
He'd hardly done anything during practice except stand in line and watch Max.

121
00:06:06.882 --> 00:06:09.163
And now he was in line again, to get his uniform.

122
00:06:10.323 --> 00:06:12.965
Jonathan watched Coach Wattenbarger give Max his uniform.

123
00:06:12.985 --> 00:06:17.386
"The number one player gets to wear number one on his jersey," Jonathan murmured.

124
00:06:18.827 --> 00:06:21.308
Jonathan's own uniform had number zero on it.

125
00:06:21.940 --> 00:06:27.344
He held up his jersey next to Max's and joked, "Look—here are the hero and the zero."

126
00:06:29.866 --> 00:06:32.648
Carlos and some other boys laughed, but Max rolled his eyes.

127
00:06:32.668 --> 00:06:38.752
"Max Wattenbarger is a great soccer player," Jonathan thought, "but he has no sense of humor."

128
00:06:40.013 --> 00:06:44.756
If they were on a sense-of-humor team together, Jonathan would be number one and Max would be zero.

129
00:06:45.897 --> 00:06:48.398
Then it was Jonathan's turn to roll his eyes—at himself.

130
00:06:49.039 --> 00:06:50.480
They were not on a sense-of-humor team.

131
00:06:51.352 --> 00:06:52.353
They were on a soccer team.

132
00:06:52.973 --> 00:06:56.696
And it was a soccer team with his best friend—and with the best player in the league.

133
00:06:56.716 --> 00:06:59.979
"So you're actually really lucky," he told himself.

134
00:06:59.999 --> 00:07:02.280
"It's going to be a fantastic season."
